{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>My lord asked, saying.</b> The reason for prefacing these words is to say that it was under compulsion that they took Binyamin from his father, and if he does not see him with them his father will die of his anguish. And he began by saying <b>my lord asked his servants</b> — meaning: this was not the questioning of an ordinary man like himself who could be prevented from receiving an answer; rather, it came from my lord to his servants, and since that is so, it is perforce <b>to say</b> to you the truth of the matter. It further intends, in his saying <b>to say</b>, that besides the questioning you conducted against us, you did something that obligates us to tell you without concealment — for you treated them as spies, and they were required to verify their words as is the procedure in interrogating men suspected of espionage, who are investigated in every detail even when those details are irrelevant to the matter of espionage, and if they conceal anything they are held accountable (lit. placed in the collar) — therefore he compelled them to say."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:48:36.377208076Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}